  "id": "ENT094",
  "title": "The Elevator Button Courtesy Loop",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "everyday microdramas",
  "premise": "Two neighbors each insist the other should choose the destination first, leaving a toy lift motionless through an elaborate polite exchange. One draws two floor numbers on a card, both point to the same number, and they press it together before bowing themselves almost out of the frame.",
  "hook": "After you. After you. Still after you.",
  "visible_action": "Hands hover over buttons; bows deepen; card appears; two fingers land on the same number; lift display finally changes.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A tiny explicit choice can resolve excessive politeness.",
  "gate": "Fictional lift interaction; no operational or emergency elevator advice.",
